cl builds `Plain many[2];` by calling its own runtime helper, the vector constructor iterator ??_H@YAXPEAX_K1P6APEAX0@Z@Z, and passing it the element constructor; cxx1 emits the loop inline. So cl's object names a helper cxx1's does not. It is the same difference array-of-class.nocl records, met again here because this case constructs an array to prove the array path marks the implicit constructor used. Neither is an ABI question - nothing outside the object can tell which was used - and cxx1 has no such helper to call, the runtime it links against being whatever the platform provides rather than a library of its own.
